This Python module works with money values.

To parse a money amount from some text:
    remove any leading dollar sign and any commas from the text
    turn what remains into a number
    give back that number rounded to 2 decimals as a numeric value (not formatted text)

To format a money amount:
    give back the amount as text like "$1,234.50": a dollar sign,
    thousands separated by commas, and always 2 decimals

For example, parsing "$1,299.99" must give 1299.99.
Parsing "54.20" must give the numeric value 54.2 (equivalent to 54.20).
Formatting 1234.5 must give exactly "$1,234.50".
Formatting 15.5 must give exactly "$15.50".
